{"name":"Birdie","hex":"#e9e424","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Birdie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from English.","A name for any (small) bird. (1999: Oxford Dictionary of Slang, p. 130)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Birdie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Birdie, Georgia","blocks":[{"text":"Birdie is an unincorporated community in Spalding County, in the U.S. state of Georgia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birdie%2C_Georgia","wikidata":"Q43080656"},{"title":"Birdie, Mississippi","blocks":[{"text":"Birdie is an unincorporated community in Quitman County, Mississippi. Birdie is located on Mississippi Highway 315, northwest of Marks."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birdie%2C_Mississippi","wikidata":"Q4915986"},{"title":"Birdie (Street Fighter)","blocks":[{"text":"Birdie  is a character in the Street Fighter series. He first appeared in the original Street Fighter game in 1987 as a non-playable opponent before becoming playable in Street Fighter Alpha and the subsequent Alpha games. He was originally depicted with light skin in the original game, but is depicted with dark skin in Alpha, with the explanation being that he was pale due to an illness. He later appeared in Street Fighter V, though his design was made more fat compared to his Alpha design."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/Street_Fighter_Alpha_Birdie.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birdie_(Street_Fighter)","wikidata":"Q3272904"},{"title":"Birdie (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Birdie is the 2015 debut novel of Indigenous Canadian author Tracey Lindberg. It was first published in hardback on May 26, 2015, by HarperCollins Publishers. Upon its release it was named a CBC Canada Reads Finalist, OLA Evergreen Award and a KOBO Emerging Writer Prize. The book is known for its inclusion of Cree Law and its commentary on Canadian Colonialism."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Birdie_%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birdie_(novel)","wikidata":"Q65082511"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Restaurant Amigos de Acapulco (window), Chico","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Restaurant_Amigos_de_Acapulco_%28window%29%2C_Chico.jpg/500px-Restaurant_Amigos_de_Acapulco_%28window%29%2C_Chico.jpg","ratio":1.5496983169260083,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Restaurant_Amigos_de_Acapulco_(window),_Chico.jpg","share":0.275625},{"title":"Hoverfly January 2008-6","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Hoverfly_January_2008-6.jpg/500px-Hoverfly_January_2008-6.jpg","ratio":1.250655021834061,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hoverfly_January_2008-6.jpg","share":0.26875},{"title":"Etymology of a Classical Meitei language term for “yellow colour”","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg/500px-Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","share":0.085},{"title":"Portulaca grandiflora, Burdwan, 31032014 (2)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Portulaca_grandiflora%2C_Burdwan%2C_31032014_%282%29.jpg/500px-Portulaca_grandiflora%2C_Burdwan%2C_31032014_%282%29.jpg","ratio":1.5056179775280898,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portulaca_grandiflora,_Burdwan,_31032014_(2).jpg","share":0.074375},{"title":"Yellow Portulaca flower in sunshine, on black background","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ye